# CD-149 session, 2026-08-16 — Principal-approved (tools-class).
#
# The repo stores LF. Windows checkouts were writing CRLF back into the working tree, and with
# core.autocrlf unset and no attributes file, git reported 216 files as modified with 54,628
# insertions against 54,628 deletions and ZERO real content change. That noise BLOCKED a pull:
# eight of the files an incoming commit touched were "locally modified", so git refused the merge.
#
# EXISTING CHECKOUTS NORMALIZE ON NEXT TOUCH, not on adding this file. A working tree that already
# holds CRLF keeps holding it until each file is rewritten; `git add --renormalize .` does it in
# one step if the noise reappears before then.
* text=auto eol=lf
